Jellyfin test server with music and Live TV (docs/testing.md, "Test server").

    scripts/test-server/up.sh     # media (first time), 4 live channels, Jellyfin on port 8097, set-up
    scripts/test-server/down.sh   # stops everything; data kept in ~/.local/share/playfin-testserver

Sign in as "playfin" / "playfin-test" (local test server only). Remove ~/.local/share/playfin-testserver to start
from scratch.

For the console: STREAMS=<this PC's address>:8098 scripts/test-server/up.sh puts the channels' own address in the
M3U list, so that Playfin plays them directly from the PC (port 8098) rather than through Jellyfin. The console's
own TV guide (Settings > TV guide) is http://<this PC's address>:8098/console-guide.xml: it describes channel 4,
"Playfin Direct", which the server's guide leaves empty.

Showcase: SHOWCASE=1 scripts/test-server/up.sh (and SHOWCASE=1 down.sh) runs the same server with real content
instead, in ~/.local/share/playfin-showcase: free albums from the Internet Archive and TV channels streamed for
free by their broadcasters, with their logos and real programmes (make-showcase.py; credits in
scripts/showcase/CREDITS.md). Stop the other one first: both use ports 8097 and 8098.
